      en: "San Jose Church of Cedros is a notable location in Honduras that reflects the country's geographic and cultural diversity. A historical church in the town of Cedros, where the first Constituent Assembly of Honduras took place in 1824. At the same time birthplace of democracy in hn. In addition colonial heritage. In the surrounding area central importance. In this way, San Jose Church of Cedros fits naturally into the wider picture of Honduras, showing how closely linked nature, history and economy are across the country."
