      en: "El Puente is an archaeological site of the Maya civilization located in western Honduras, near the Copán River. It flourished between 600 and 900 AD as a key trading hub connecting the Copán region with the Motagua Valley. Excavations have revealed a central plaza, residential compounds, and a ball court. The architecture exhibits both Classic Maya and local stylistic influences. Artifacts such as obsidian blades, jade ornaments, and polychrome pottery indicate long-distance trade. The site is part of a protected archaeological park, attracting researchers and tourists interested in pre-Columbian history.",
